{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-7 ruling on 0d069729. The condition moves to the first head with\nboth capabilities. That head is NF-5 after CF-1 is on main.\n\nCorrection of my ruling e2e0989b. I took option (a) because I read\nthat no user reaches the Counter page after the cutover deployment.\nThe CF-1 head says the reverse: a room of the `base` cohort installs\nan ordinary package such as Counter (`docs/deploy.md:374` at\n4369fddf). So the Counter page is a user path after the deployment,\nand the join witness does not stand for it.\n\n1. CF-1 carries nothing of NF-5 and nothing of NF-7. Its gate and\n   its review go on as they are. File the CF-1 review when the gate\n   passes.\n2. NF-5 keeps its gate slot. After CF-1 lands, NF-5 takes main, and\n   its `custody-witness.mjs` gains a Counter half that runs. The\n   Counter half runs with no failure before the NF-5 review request,\n   and that request names NF-7. The five facts of NF-7 are the\n   witness.\n3. The preparation is the path of `docs/deploy.md`, \"application\n   packages\", with no test-only install path:\n   - `dap pack` the Counter package at the NF-5 head, with a\n     publisher key made for the witness in a scratch home. Use no\n     operator home.\n   - Commit the packet on the NF-5 branch and push it. The\n     repository is public, so the commit is an immutable Git URI on\n     `github.com`.\n   - The local celld Worker gets `APPLICATION_TRUST` with that\n     release, publisher and host, and a local `APPLICATION_CONTENT`\n     bucket.\n   - A room of the `base` cohort installs the package with\n     `dap install`, and the browser opens its Counter.\n   If one step cannot run on a local Worker, send me the step and\n   the reason before you build a way around it.\n4. The NF-5 review request no longer names a blocker for Counter.\n   It still names the Counter Node witnesses.\n\nI change the conditions of NF-7 by this act: the NF-5 head, after\nCF-1, carries the witness.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}